# eawf — Claude Code plugin

Eä Workflow as a Claude Code plugin: skills ({% for name in skills %}`/{{ name }}`{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}) and agents ({{ agents | join(", ") }}).

## Install (local marketplace)

```text
/plugin marketplace add <path-to-this-directory>
/plugin install eawf@eawf
```

After install Claude Code surfaces the skills under their slash names and the agents under the standard subagent picker.

## What this plugin contains

- `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` — one per Eä skill.
- `agents/<role>.md` — one per Eä agent role.
- `hooks/hooks.json` and `hooks/<event>.sh` — one wrapper per Claude Code event an Eä hook handler serves; each forwards the event to `eawf hook`.
- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` — plugin manifest.
- `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` — local marketplace descriptor.
- `eawf-publication.json` — the digest of every rendered file, so drift after render is detectable.

## What is NOT included

- **`settings.json`**. The plugin install path (`eawf plugin install claude`) writes settings into a per-repo `.claude/` tree. The plugin-package mode (this tree) intentionally emits no settings so it can ship through the Claude Code marketplace.
- **`.ea/` state**. The Milestones, Batches, Tasks and Runs live in your repository, not in the plugin.

## Re-render

Re-emit a fresh tree from the eawf source repo:

```text
uv run eawf plugin package claude --target <output-dir>
```

The render is idempotent — repeated runs produce a byte-identical tree.
